Z||000000||pHoOl||11-25-2001||07:48 PM||||Okay... i love this forum as much as everybody else... but there is one aspect about it (or maybe just the people on it) that is starting to bother me. <P>Why is it that people feel they need to be nasty about telling people where a post should be.  I'd understand if the first person to respond said something like "btw, in the future this is more suited for off topic" or something of the sort... but people are just getting nasty about it.  One post i read a few minutes ago had a response of " Oh.. sorry, didn't realize i clicked on the mall, i thought i clicked on general fiero info".  Why??? do people actually feel good about themselves by being asses about it?   <P>A post i read a few weeks ago had someone respond twice within like five posts about how it was aweful that it was posted in the wrong section.  People... the world isn't going to end if someone accidently posts in the wrong section.  Furthermore... i haven't seen a place to change where it's posted.  i think cliff can, but not aware that any of the rest of us can.  So why keep posting that their post is in the wrong section??  i think they get the idea after the first time.<P><BR>Okay... i'm done.  i feel better now<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
